# Migration files carry a sqlx checksum: `sqlx::migrate!` hashes each file's
# bytes at build time and the runner compares that hash against what it recorded
# in `_sqlx_migrations`. Any byte that moves -- including an EOL conversion --
# makes a deployment that already ran the migration refuse to start with
# "migration <version> was previously applied but has been modified".
#
# Pin them to LF so the working copy, a fresh clone, and the Linux image build
# all see identical bytes. Without this, core.autocrlf=true materialises CRLF on
# Windows and the same migration has two different hashes depending on the
# machine that ran it.
#
# What may not change is the content: see scripts/check-migrations.py, which
# fails CI when a migration that already shipped was edited or deleted.
*.sql text eol=lf
